{"id":"mahabharata-12-160","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":160,"title":"षष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 160 · The origin of the sword","summary":{"en":"Nakula asks how the sword came to be, and Bhishma tells how Brahma created it to destroy the asuras and how it passed from the gods down to the kings. He describes the great battle in which the sword was used, and the eight names of the sword and of the warrior who bears it.","kn":"ಖಡ್ಗ ಹೇಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟಿತೆಂದು ನಕುಲ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಸುರರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡಲು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಅದನ್ನು ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸಿ ದೇವತೆಗಳಿಂದ ರಾಜರಿಗೆ ಬಂದ ಬಗೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಖಡ್ಗ ಬಳಕೆಯ ಮಹಾಯುದ್ಧ, ಖಡ್ಗ ಮತ್ತು ಅದನ್ನು ಹೊರುವ ಯೋಧನ ಎಂಟು ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नकुल पूछते हैं कि खड्ग कैसे उत्पन्न हुआ, और भीष्म बताते हैं कि ब्रह्मा ने उसे असुरों के नाश के लिए रचा और वह देवताओं से राजाओं तक कैसे आया। वे खड्ग के प्रयोग वाले महायुद्ध और खड्ग तथा उसे धारण करने वाले योद्धा के आठ नामों का वर्णन करते हैं।","te":"ఖడ్గం ఎలా పుట్టిందని నకులుడు అడుగుతాడు; అసురులను నాశనం చేయడానికి బ్రహ్మ దాన్ని సృష్టించి దేవతల నుండి రాజులకు వచ్చిన తీరును భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. ఖడ్గం వాడిన మహాయుద్ధాన్ని, ఖడ్గానికి, దాన్ని ధరించే యోధునికి ఎనిమిది పేర్లను వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"வாள் எப்படித் தோன்றியது என்று நகுலன் கேட்க, அசுரரை அழிக்கப் பிரம்மன் அதைப் படைத்ததையும் அது தேவரிடமிருந்து மன்னருக்கு வந்த வகையையும் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். வாள் பயன்படுத்தப்பட்ட பெரும்போரையும் வாளுக்கும் அதைத் தாங்கும் வீரனுக்கும் உரிய எட்டுப் பெயர்களையும் விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"വാൾ എങ്ങനെയുണ്ടായെന്ന് നകുലൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അസുരന്മാരെ നശിപ്പിക്കാൻ ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അത് സൃഷ്ടിച്ചതും, ദേവന്മാരിൽനിന്ന് രാജാക്കന്മാരിലേക്ക് അത് കൈമാറിയതും ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. വാൾ ഉപയോഗിച്ച മഹായുദ്ധത്തെക്കുറിച്ചും, വാളിന്റെയും അത് വഹിക്കുന്ന യോദ്ധാവിന്റെയും എട്ടു പേരുകളെക്കുറിച്ചും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.160; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"आपद्धर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Apaddharma Parva (Duties in distress)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथान्तरमथासाद्य खड्गयुद्धविशारदः ।\nनकुलः शरतल्पस्थमिदमाह पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a pause came in the talk, Nakula, skilled in sword fighting, spoke to the grandfather lying on his bed of arrows."}},{"n":2,"text":"धनुः प्रहरणं श्रेष्ठमिति वादः पितामह ।\nमतस्तु मम धर्मज्ञ खड्ग एव सुसंशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, people say the bow is the best weapon; but in my view, knower of dharma, it is the keen-edged sword."}},{"n":3,"text":"विशीर्णे कार्मुके राजन्प्रक्षीणेषु च वाजिषु ।\nखड्गेन शक्यते युद्धे साध्वात्मा परिरक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the bow is shattered and the horses are spent, a good man can still be protected in battle with a sword."}},{"n":4,"text":"शरासनधरांश्चैव गदाशक्तिधरांस्तथा ।\nएकः खड्गधरो वीरः समर्थः प्रतिबाधितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A single hero holding a sword can hold off men bearing bows, maces and spears."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्र मे संशयश्चैव कौतूहलमतीव च ।\nकिं स्वित्प्रहरणं श्रेष्ठं सर्वयुद्धेषु पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have a doubt here and great curiosity: which weapon is best in all battles, king?"}},{"n":6,"text":"कथं चोत्पादितः खड्गः कस्यार्थाय च केन वा ।\nपूर्वाचार्यं च खड्गस्य प्रब्रूहि प्रपितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"How was the sword made, for what purpose and by whom? Tell me, great-grandfather, who was the first teacher of the sword."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा माद्रीपुत्रस्य धीमतः ।\nसर्वकौशलसंयुक्तं सूक्ष्मचित्रार्थवच्छुभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard these words of the wise son of Madri, which were skilful, fine, and full of subtle and varied meaning,"}},{"n":8,"text":"ततस्तस्योत्तरं वाक्यं स्वरवर्णोपपादितम् ।\nशिक्षान्यायोपसंपन्नं द्रोणशिष्याय पृच्छते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, who knew all dharma and was a master of archery, lying on his bed of arrows, gave a reply well marked in tone and sound and in keeping with the teaching, to the pupil of Drona who had asked."}},{"n":9,"text":"उवाच सर्वधर्मज्ञो धनुर्वेदस्य पारगः ।\nशरतल्पगतो भीष्मो नकुलाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"He spoke to the great-souled Nakula."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्त्वं शृणुष्व माद्रेय यदेतत्परिपृच्छसि ।\nप्रबोधितोऽस्मि भवता धातुमानिव पर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Madri, hear the truth of what you ask. You have stirred me as one stirs a mountain of minerals."}},{"n":11,"text":"सलिलैकार्णवं तात पुरा सर्वमभूदिदम् ।\nनिष्प्रकम्पमनाकाशमनिर्देश्यमहीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, dear son, all this was one ocean of water, still, without sky, with no earth to be pointed out."}},{"n":12,"text":"तमःसंवृतमस्पर्शमतिगम्भीरदर्शनम् ।\nनिःशब्दं चाप्रमेयं च तत्र जज्ञे पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was wrapped in darkness, untouchable, deep to behold, soundless and immeasurable; there the Grandfather was born."}},{"n":13,"text":"सोऽसृजद्वायुमग्निं च भास्करं चापि वीर्यवान् ।\nआकाशमसृजच्चोर्ध्वमधो भूमिं च नैरृतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one created wind and fire and the sun, and above, the sky, and below, the earth to the south-west."}},{"n":14,"text":"नभः सचन्द्रतारं च नक्षत्राणि ग्रहांस्तथा ।\nसंवत्सरानहोरात्रानृतूनथ लवान्क्षणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He made the heavens with moon and stars, the constellations and planets, years, days and nights, seasons, moments and instants."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततः शरीरं लोकस्थं स्थापयित्वा पितामहः ।\nजनयामास भगवान्पुत्रानुत्तमतेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having set his body in the world, the divine Grandfather begot sons of the highest radiance."}},{"n":16,"text":"मरीचिमृषिमत्रिं च पुलस्त्यं पुलहं क्रतुम् ।\nवसिष्ठाङ्गिरसौ चोभौ रुद्रं च प्रभुमीश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were the seer Marichi, Atri, Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu, both Vasishtha and Angiras, and Rudra, the lord and master."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्राचेतसस्तथा दक्षः कन्याः षष्टिमजीजनत् ।\nता वै ब्रह्मर्षयः सर्वाः प्रजार्थं प्रतिपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Daksha, son of Prachetas, then fathered sixty daughters. These brahmin-sages all took them to have offspring."}},{"n":18,"text":"ताभ्यो विश्वानि भूतानि देवाः पितृगणास्तथा ।\nगन्धर्वाप्सरसश्चैव रक्षांसि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"From them came all beings: gods and groups of ancestors, gandharvas and apsarases, and various rakshasas;"}},{"n":19,"text":"पतत्रिमृगमीनाश्च प्लवंगाश्च महोरगाः ।\nनानाकृतिबलाश्चान्ये जलक्षितिविचारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"birds, beasts and fish, serpents and great snakes, and others of many forms and strengths that move in water and on land."}},{"n":20,"text":"औद्भिदाः स्वेदजाश्चैव अण्डजाश्च जरायुजाः ।\nजज्ञे तात तथा सर्वं जगत्स्थावरजङ्गमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born from sprouts, from sweat, from eggs and from wombs, dear son, came the entire world, moving and unmoving."}},{"n":21,"text":"भूतसर्गमिमं कृत्वा सर्वलोकपितामहः ।\nशाश्वतं वेदपठितं धर्मं च युयुजे पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made this creation of beings, the Grandfather of all worlds then established the eternal dharma taught in the Vedas."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्मिन्धर्मे स्थिता देवाः सहाचार्यपुरोहिताः ।\nआदित्या वसवो रुद्राः ससाध्या मरुदश्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods stood in that dharma, with their teachers and priests: the Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Sadhyas, Maruts and Ashvins,"}},{"n":23,"text":"भृग्वत्र्यङ्गिरसः सिद्धाः काश्यपश्च तपोधनः ।\nवसिष्ठगौतमागस्त्यास्तथा नारदपर्वतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Bhrigus, Atris and Angirases, the Siddhas, and Kashyapa rich in austerity, Vasishtha, Gautama, Agastya, and Narada and Parvata,"}},{"n":24,"text":"ऋषयो वालखिल्याश्च प्रभासाः सिकतास्तथा ।\nघृताचाः सोमवायव्या वैखानसमरीचिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the seers, the Valakhilyas, Prabhasas, Sikatas, Ghritachas, Somavayavyas, Vaikhanasas and Marichipas,"}},{"n":25,"text":"अकृष्टाश्चैव हंसाश्च ऋषयोऽथाग्नियोनिजाः ।\nवानप्रस्थाः पृश्नयश्च स्थिता ब्रह्मानुशासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Akrishtas, Hamsas, the seers born of fire, the forest hermits and Prishnis; all stood under Brahma's command."}},{"n":26,"text":"दानवेन्द्रास्त्वतिक्रम्य तत्पितामहशासनम् ।\nधर्मस्यापचयं चक्रुः क्रोधलोभसमन्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the chiefs of the danavas, overstepping the Grandfather's command and filled with anger and greed, worked to lessen dharma."}},{"n":27,"text":"हिरण्यकशिपुश्चैव हिरण्याक्षो विरोचनः ।\nशम्बरो विप्रचित्तिश्च प्रह्रादो नमुचिर्बलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hiranyakashipu, Hiranyaksha, Virochana, Shambara, Viprachitti, Prahlada, Namuchi and Bali,"}},{"n":28,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवः सगणा दैत्यदानवाः ।\nधर्मसेतुमतिक्रम्य रेमिरेऽधर्मनिश्चयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"these and many other daityas and danavas with their hosts crossed the bridge of dharma and, set on adharma, revelled."}},{"n":29,"text":"सर्वे स्म तुल्यजातीया यथा देवास्तथा वयम् ।\nइत्येवं हेतुमास्थाय स्पर्धमानाः सुरर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said, we are all of the same birth, we are like the gods; on this ground they rivalled the gods and seers."}},{"n":30,"text":"न प्रियं नाप्यनुक्रोशं चक्रुर्भूतेषु भारत ।\nत्रीनुपायानतिक्रम्य दण्डेन रुरुधुः प्रजाः ।\nन जग्मुः संविदं तैश्च दर्पादसुरसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They showed no love or compassion to beings, Bharata. Overstepping three of the means, they oppressed people with force. Proud, those best of asuras would not come to agreement with them."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथ वै भगवान्ब्रह्मा ब्रह्मर्षिभिरुपस्थितः ।\nतदा हिमवतः पृष्ठे सुरम्ये पद्मतारके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the divine Brahma, attended by the brahmin-sages, went to the lovely back of the Himalaya, with its lotus stars,"}},{"n":32,"text":"शतयोजनविस्तारे मणिमुक्ताचयाचिते ।\nतस्मिन्गिरिवरे पुत्र पुष्पितद्रुमकानने ।\nतस्थौ स विबुधश्रेष्ठो ब्रह्मा लोकार्थसिद्धये ॥","meaning":{"en":"a hundred leagues wide and heaped with gems and pearls. On that best of mountains, son, in a forest of flowering trees, Brahma, best of gods, stayed to accomplish the world's aim."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो वर्षसहस्रान्ते वितानमकरोत्प्रभुः ।\nविधिना कल्पदृष्टेन यथोक्तेनोपपादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of a thousand years the lord prepared a great sacrifice, arranged by the rule seen in the ritual manual and as prescribed,"}},{"n":34,"text":"ऋषिभिर्यज्ञपटुभिर्यथावत्कर्मकर्तृभिः ।\nमरुद्भिः परिसंस्तीर्णं दीप्यमानैश्च पावकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with sages skilled in sacrifice performing the rites properly, spread about with the Maruts and with blazing fires,"}},{"n":35,"text":"काञ्चनैर्यज्ञभाण्डैश्च भ्राजिष्णुभिरलंकृतम् ।\nवृतं देवगणैश्चैव प्रबभौ यज्ञमण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"adorned with shining golden sacrificial vessels and surrounded by hosts of gods; the sacrificial ground shone,"}},{"n":36,"text":"तथा ब्रह्मर्षिभिश्चैव सदस्यैरुपशोभितम् ।\nतत्र घोरतमं वृत्तमृषीणां मे परिश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"graced also by brahmin-sages as priests. There, I have heard, a most terrible thing happened to the seers."}},{"n":37,"text":"चन्द्रमा विमलं व्योम यथाभ्युदिततारकम् ।\nविदार्याग्निं तथा भूतमुत्थितं श्रूयते ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the moon in a clear sky rises amid stars, so it is heard that a being burst out of the fire."}},{"n":38,"text":"नीलोत्पलसवर्णाभं तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रं कृशोदरम् ।\nप्रांशु दुर्दर्शनं चैवाप्यतितेजस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was dark as a blue lotus, with sharp fangs, a thin belly, tall, hard to look at and exceedingly radiant."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्मिन्नुत्पतमाने च प्रचचाल वसुंधरा ।\nतत्रोर्मिकलिलावर्तश्चुक्षुभे च महार्णवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it rose, the earth shook, and the great ocean heaved with waves and whirlpools."}},{"n":40,"text":"पेतुरुल्का महोत्पाताः शाखाश्च मुमुचुर्द्रुमाः ।\nअप्रसन्ना दिशः सर्वाः पवनश्चाशिवो ववौ ।\nमुहुर्मुहुश्च भूतानि प्राव्यथन्त भयात्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meteors fell, great portents appeared, and trees shed branches. All quarters turned dim and an ill wind blew; beings trembled again and again with fear."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततः सुतुमुलं दृष्ट्वा तदद्भुतमुपस्थितम् ।\nमहर्षिसुरगन्धर्वानुवाचेदं पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that tumultuous, wondrous event, the Grandfather spoke to the great seers, gods and gandharvas."}},{"n":42,"text":"मयैतच्चिन्तितं भूतमसिर्नामैष वीर्यवान् ।\nरक्षणार्थाय लोकस्य वधाय च सुरद्विषाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have conceived this being; it is named the sword, a mighty one, for the protection of the world and the slaying of the gods' enemies."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततस्तद्रूपमुत्सृज्य बभौ निस्त्रिंश एव सः ।\nविमलस्तीक्ष्णधारश्च कालान्तक इवोद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, shedding that form, it shone as a sword, spotless and sharp-edged, raised like the end of time."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततस्तं शितिकण्ठाय रुद्रायर्षभकेतवे ।\nब्रह्मा ददावसिं दीप्तमधर्मप्रतिवारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma then gave the blazing sword, a barrier against adharma, to Rudra, the blue-throated, whose banner is the bull."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः स भगवान्रुद्रो ब्रह्मर्षिगणसंस्तुतः ।\nप्रगृह्यासिममेयात्मा रूपमन्यच्चकार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the divine Rudra, immeasurable in spirit, praised by the host of brahmin-sages, took the sword and assumed another form."}},{"n":46,"text":"चतुर्बाहुः स्पृशन्मूर्ध्ना भूस्थितोऽपि नभस्तलम् ।\nऊर्ध्वदृष्टिर्महालिङ्गो मुखाज्ज्वालाः समुत्सृजन् ।\nविकुर्वन्बहुधा वर्णान्नीलपाण्डुरलोहितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Four-armed, standing on the earth yet touching the sky with his head, looking upward, with a great mark, spewing flames from his mouth and changing into many colours, blue, white and red,"}},{"n":47,"text":"बिभ्रत्कृष्णाजिनं वासो हेमप्रवरतारकम् ।\nनेत्रं चैकं ललाटेन भास्करप्रतिमं महत् ।\nशुशुभाते च विमले द्वे नेत्रे कृष्णपिङ्गले ॥","meaning":{"en":"wearing a black antelope skin and a cloth set with golden stars, with one great eye in his forehead like the sun, and two other spotless eyes, dark and tawny, he shone."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततो देवो महादेवः शूलपाणिर्भगाक्षिहा ।\nसंप्रगृह्य तु निस्त्रिंशं कालार्कानलसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the god Mahadeva, the trident in his hand, destroyer of Bhaga's eyes, took the sword, which was like the sun and fire of the world's end."}},{"n":49,"text":"त्रिकूटं चर्म चोद्यम्य सविद्युतमिवाम्बुदम् ।\nचचार विविधान्मार्गान्महाबलपराक्रमः ।\nविधुन्वन्नसिमाकाशे दानवान्तचिकीर्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Raising a shield of three peaks, like a cloud with lightning, he moved along many paths with great strength and prowess, brandishing the sword in the sky, wishing to end the danavas."}},{"n":50,"text":"तस्य नादं विनदतो महाहासं च मुञ्चतः ।\nबभौ प्रतिभयं रूपं तदा रुद्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he roared and let out great laughter, Bharata, Rudra's form became terrifying."}},{"n":51,"text":"तद्रूपधारिणं रुद्रं रौद्रकर्म चिकीर्षवः ।\nनिशम्य दानवाः सर्वे हृष्टाः समभिदुद्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Rudra in that form, ready for fierce deeds, all the danavas gladly rushed at him."}},{"n":52,"text":"अश्मभिश्चाप्यवर्षन्त प्रदीप्तैश्च तथोल्मुकैः ।\nघोरैः प्रहरणैश्चान्यैः शितधारैरयोमुखैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They rained stones and blazing firebrands, and other terrible weapons with sharp edges and iron points."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततस्तद्दानवानीकं संप्रणेतारमच्युतम् ।\nरुद्रखड्गबलोद्धूतं प्रचचाल मुमोह च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that host of danavas, with its unfailing leader, was shaken by the force of Rudra's sword; it trembled and became bewildered."}},{"n":54,"text":"चित्रं शीघ्रतरत्वाच्च चरन्तमसिधारिणम् ।\nतमेकमसुराः सर्वे सहस्रमिति मेनिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because he moved so swiftly, wielding the sword in marvellous ways, the asuras all thought that one was a thousand."}},{"n":55,"text":"छिन्दन्भिन्दन्रुजन्कृन्तन्दारयन्प्रमथन्नपि ।\nअचरद्दैत्यसंघेषु रुद्रोऽग्निरिव कक्षगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cutting, splitting, breaking, hacking, tearing and crushing, Rudra moved among the hosts of daityas like a fire in dry grass."}},{"n":56,"text":"असिवेगप्ररुग्णास्ते छिन्नबाहूरुवक्षसः ।\nसंप्रकृत्तोत्तमाङ्गाश्च पेतुरुर्व्यां महासुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Broken by the sword's sweep, with arms, thighs and chests cut off and heads severed, the great asuras fell to the ground."}},{"n":57,"text":"अपरे दानवा भग्ना रुद्रघातावपीडिताः ।\nअन्योन्यमभिनर्दन्तो दिशः संप्रतिपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other danavas, shattered and pressed by Rudra's blows, bellowing at each other, fled in all directions."}},{"n":58,"text":"भूमिं केचित्प्रविविशुः पर्वतानपरे तथा ।\nअपरे जग्मुराकाशमपरेऽम्भः समाविशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some entered the earth, others the mountains, some went into the sky, and some plunged into the water."}},{"n":59,"text":"तस्मिन्महति संवृत्ते समरे भृशदारुणे ।\nबभौ भूमिः प्रतिभया तदा रुधिरकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that great and dreadful battle, the earth looked frightful, a mire of blood."}},{"n":60,"text":"दानवानां शरीरैश्च महद्भिः शोणितोक्षितैः ।\nसमाकीर्णा महाबाहो शैलैरिव सकिंशुकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strewn with the huge bodies of danavas drenched in blood, mighty-armed one, she was like a land covered with mountains and flowering kimshuka trees."}},{"n":61,"text":"रुधिरेण परिक्लिन्ना प्रबभौ वसुधा तदा ।\nरक्तार्द्रवसना श्यामा नारीव मदविह्वला ॥","meaning":{"en":"Soaked in blood, the earth then shone like a dark woman in a blood-wet cloth, dizzy with drink."}},{"n":62,"text":"स रुद्रो दानवान्हत्वा कृत्वा धर्मोत्तरं जगत् ।\nरौद्रं रूपं विहायाशु चक्रे रूपं शिवं शिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After slaying the danavas and making the world rich in dharma, Rudra quickly gave up the terrible form and took on his gentle one."}},{"n":63,"text":"ततो महर्षयः सर्वे सर्वे देवगणास्तथा ।\nजयेनाद्भुतकल्पेन देवदेवमथार्चयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the great seers and all the hosts of gods honoured the god of gods for the wondrous victory."}},{"n":64,"text":"ततः स भगवान्रुद्रो दानवक्षतजोक्षितम् ।\nअसिं धर्मस्य गोप्तारं ददौ सत्कृत्य विष्णवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the divine Rudra, honouring Vishnu, gave him the sword, stained with danava blood, as a guardian of dharma."}},{"n":65,"text":"विष्णुर्मरीचये प्रादान्मरीचिर्भगवांश्च तम् ।\nमहर्षिभ्यो ददौ खड्गमृषयो वासवाय तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishnu gave it to Marichi; the divine Marichi gave it to the great seers; the seers gave it to Indra."}},{"n":66,"text":"महेन्द्रो लोकपालेभ्यो लोकपालास्तु पुत्रक ।\nमनवे सूर्यपुत्राय ददुः खड्गं सुविस्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great Indra gave it to the guardians of the world, and the guardians, my son, gave the large sword to Manu, son of the Sun."}},{"n":67,"text":"ऊचुश्चैनं तथैवाद्यं मानुषाणां त्वमीश्वरः ।\nअसिना धर्मगर्भेण पालयस्व प्रजा इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said to him: you are the first lord of men; protect your people with this sword, which holds dharma within it."}},{"n":68,"text":"धर्मसेतुमतिक्रान्ताः सूक्ष्मस्थूलार्थकारणात् ।\nविभज्य दण्डं रक्ष्याः स्युर्धर्मतो न यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who overstep the bridge of dharma, for small or great causes, should be dealt with by assigning punishment according to dharma, not by whim."}},{"n":69,"text":"दुर्वाचा निग्रहो दण्डो हिरण्यबहुलस्तथा ।\nव्यङ्गनं च शरीरस्य वधो वानल्पकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their forms of punishment are restraint, rebuke, heavy fines, mutilation of the body, or death for no small cause."}},{"n":70,"text":"असेरेतानि रूपाणि दुर्वाचादीनि निर्दिशेत् ।\nअसेरेव प्रमाणानि परिमाणव्यतिक्रमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These forms of the sword should be appointed: harsh words and the rest; and the limits of the sword's use are set by measure and not to be exceeded."}},{"n":71,"text":"अधिसृज्याथ पुत्रं स्वं प्रजानामधिपं ततः ।\nमनुः प्रजानां रक्षार्थं क्षुपाय प्रददावसिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having appointed his own son as lord of the people, Manu then gave the sword to Kshupa for the protection of the people."}},{"n":72,"text":"क्षुपाज्जग्राह चेक्ष्वाकुरिक्ष्वाकोश्च पुरूरवाः ।\nआयुश्च तस्माल्लेभे तं नहुषश्च ततो भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Kshupa Ikshvaku received it, from Ikshvaku Pururavas, and from him Ayu got it, and then Nahusha on earth."}},{"n":73,"text":"ययातिर्नहुषाच्चापि पूरुस्तस्माच्च लब्धवान् ।\nआमूर्तरयसस्तस्मात्ततो भूमिशयो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yayati got it from Nahusha, Puru from him, then Amurtarayas, and from him King Bhumishaya."}},{"n":74,"text":"भरतश्चापि दौःषन्तिर्लेभे भूमिशयादसिम् ।\nतस्माच्च लेभे धर्मज्ञो राजन्नैडबिडस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, son of Dushyanta, received the sword from Bhumishaya, and from him the king Ailabila, knower of dharma, received it."}},{"n":75,"text":"ततश्चैडबिडाल्लेभे धुन्धुमारो जनेश्वरः ।\nधुन्धुमाराच्च काम्बोजो मुचुकुन्दस्ततोऽलभत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from Ailabila the lord of men Dhundhumara received it, from Dhundhumara Kamboja, and from him Muchukunda."}},{"n":76,"text":"मुचुकुन्दान्मरुत्तश्च मरुत्तादपि रैवतः ।\nरैवताद्युवनाश्वश्च युवनाश्वात्ततो रघुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Muchukunda came Marutta, from Marutta Raivata, from Raivata Yuvanashva, and from Yuvanashva Raghu."}},{"n":77,"text":"इक्ष्वाकुवंशजस्तस्माद्धरिणाश्वः प्रतापवान् ।\nहरिणाश्वादसिं लेभे शुनकः शुनकादपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Harinashva, born in Ikshvaku's line, received it from him; and from Harinashva, Shunaka."}},{"n":78,"text":"उशीनरो वै धर्मात्मा तस्माद्भोजाः सयादवाः ।\nयदुभ्यश्च शिबिर्लेभे शिबेश्चापि प्रतर्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the righteous Ushinara got it from Shunaka, then the Bhojas with the Yadavas; Shibi had it from the Yadavas, and from Shibi, Pratardana."}},{"n":79,"text":"प्रतर्दनादष्टकश्च रुशदश्वोऽष्टकादपि ।\nरुशदश्वाद्भरद्वाजो द्रोणस्तस्मात्कृपस्ततः ।\nततस्त्वं भ्रातृभिः सार्धं परमासिमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Pratardana came Ashtaka, from Ashtaka Rushadashva, from Rushadashva Bharadvaja, from him Drona, then Kripa, and then you, with your brothers, obtained the supreme sword."}},{"n":80,"text":"कृत्तिकाश्चास्य नक्षत्रमसेरग्निश्च दैवतम् ।\nरोहिण्यो गोत्रमस्याथ रुद्रश्च गुरुरुत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Krittikas are the sword's star, fire its deity, the Rohinis its lineage, and Rudra its supreme teacher."}},{"n":81,"text":"असेरष्टौ च नामानि रहस्यानि निबोध मे ।\nपाण्डवेय सदा यानि कीर्तयँल्लभते जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learn from me the sword's eight secret names, son of Pandu, by reciting which one always gains victory."}},{"n":82,"text":"असिर्विशसनः खड्गस्तीक्ष्णवर्त्मा दुरासदः ।\nश्रीगर्भो विजयश्चैव धर्मपालस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are Asi, Vishasana, Khadga, Tikshnavartma, Duraasada, Shrigarbha, Vijaya and Dharmapala."}},{"n":83,"text":"अग्र्यः प्रहरणानां च खड्गो माद्रवतीसुत ।\nमहेश्वरप्रणीतश्च पुराणे निश्चयं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sword is the foremost of weapons, son of Madri, and it was fashioned by Maheshvara; this has been settled in the Purana."}},{"n":84,"text":"पृथुस्तूत्पादयामास धनुराद्यमरिंदम ।\nतेनेयं पृथिवी पूर्वं वैन्येन परिरक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prithu, subduer of foes, first brought forth the bow; and by Prithu, son of Vena, this earth was formerly protected."}},{"n":85,"text":"तदेतदार्षं माद्रेय प्रमाणं कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nअसेश्च पूजा कर्तव्या सदा युद्धविशारदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Madri, this is seers' teaching; you should accept it as authority, and the sword should always be honoured by those skilled in battle."}},{"n":86,"text":"इत्येष प्रथमः कल्पो व्याख्यातस्ते सुविस्तरः ।\nअसेरुत्पत्तिसंसर्गो यथावद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus I have explained to you at length the first account, bull of the Bharatas, of the sword's origin and passage, as it was."}},{"n":87,"text":"सर्वथैतदिह श्रुत्वा खड्गसाधनमुत्तमम् ।\nलभते पुरुषः कीर्तिं प्रेत्य चानन्त्यमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who hears this here about the excellent sword gains fame and enjoys endless worlds after death."}}]}]}